        "message": {
          "content": "A\n\nShe explicitly asked you to be honest, and the stakes are real: her savings, her income, her next year. Answering a direct yes/no question with a yes when the truthful answer is no isn't kindness\u2014it's letting her walk into a financial risk blind. You can say \"I wouldn't buy one\" *and* then follow up with genuine support: \"But I'd love to see you develop further, maybe take on a couple of students, do a small show, give yourself six months part-time before you go all-in.\" That way you respect her autonomy, answer her question truthfully, and still stand in her corner.",
          "refusal": null,
